# GitHub token used to read pull requests (never commit a real value).
# Phada reads GITHUB_TOKEN, or GH_TOKEN when GITHUB_TOKEN is not set, from the environment only.
# A read-only token is enough: fine-grained with "Contents: Read-only" and "Pull requests:
# Read-only", or classic with the "repo" scope for private repositories. With the GitHub CLI:
#   export GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)
GITHUB_TOKEN=
